# Netlify serves a physical index.html at "/" via its own default-document
# handling *before* consulting redirect rules for that same exact path —
# a "/  /request.html  301" rule here never actually fired (confirmed live:
# curl showed a fresh, non-cached 200 for "/", not a 301). The reliable fix
# is what request.html now is: it was renamed to index.html so the public
# quote form is what's physically at the root, no rule needed for "/".
#
# This rule only keeps old /request.html links/bookmarks (including the
# og:url this app itself shipped before the rename) working.
/request.html    /    301
